Ask the system for its theme only when none is named

inlyne asked the desktop for its colour scheme at every start, through
the settings portal, even when its settings or the command line named a
theme, which is then used whatever the desktop says. Where nothing
answers, as in a headless session, the ask waited out D-Bus's timeout
before the first frame. It's now asked only for Auto, or when no theme
is named.

diff -ru a/src/opts/mod.rs b/src/opts/mod.rs
--- a/src/opts/mod.rs
+++ b/src/opts/mod.rs
@@ -85,7 +85,12 @@
         }
         #[cfg(not(test))]
         {
-            let system_color_scheme = ResolvedTheme::try_detect();
+            // The system is asked only when no theme is named, since a
+            // named one is used whatever it says, and asking waits on the
+            // desktop's settings portal, for as long as D-Bus allows where
+            // nothing answers.
+            let named = args.theme.or(config.theme).is_some_and(|theme| theme != ThemeType::Auto);
+            let system_color_scheme = if named { None } else { ResolvedTheme::try_detect() };
             Self::parse_and_load_inner(args, config, system_color_scheme)
         }
     }
